XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-14
XB-Kidux-Before: scratch
Description: Kidux learning module: BASIC, the home computer of the eighties with its guide
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module is BASIC, the language the first home computers spoke: a child
 writes a program in an editor, runs it, and sees it on a screen of the
 time, with text, drawings, colours and sound, and beside it a guide in
 the child's language that teaches it one idea at a time, with games to
 make. The interpreter is wwwBASIC, Apache-2.0, run in the browser; the
 editor and the guide are Kidux's own. Programs are saved and opened as
 files in the child's home, and nothing of it comes from the internet.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
